# Volt slimmer, rounder shape — 2026-10-30

The owner asked for a less bulky Volt with rounder shapes. The cabin crown is approximately 26 mm lower and 70 mm farther rearward at car scale, with its windscreen and rear endpoints unchanged. The sill is slightly raised and tapered, and the rear end has a deeper plan-view curve and tucked lower bumper. Wheel and handling coordinates are unchanged. The side and rear adjustments are modest; the model remains a stylized interpretation.

[Side view](evidence/volt-slim-round-2026-10-30/compatibility/side-clean.png), [front-quarter view](evidence/volt-slim-round-2026-10-30/compatibility/front-quarter-low-clean.png), and [rear-quarter view](evidence/volt-slim-round-2026-10-30/compatibility/rear-low-clean.png) show the final baked model. Sixteen clean/worn views were captured with each desktop renderer. The reference and source context include concurrent rounder hood and rear-shoulder work; the body changes were applied to its exact captured source, and those changes were preserved.

The new `electric_reference_slim_v1` asset root contains 221 prepared meshes. Its source hashes match the current builders and every listed resource exists. Racing shadows, the Electric Garage template and Garage/header/catalogue/news and 49 livery pictures were refreshed. Visible detailed/simple triangles are 119,904/34,872, with 3,250 shadow triangles.

The cabin actual-buffer fit check passed 20/20 in both procedural and prepared modes; the prepared nose/light check passed 64/64, Electric model 15/15, racing model 23/23 and actual Garage/race 58/58. The current concurrent hood has a 3.796 mm model-coordinate rise above its cowl, so the earlier hood-reference fixture passes 13/15 and fails its two no-hump assertions; a prior isolated test confirmed that those failures predate the task's five body changes. The current rear-deck/cap normals also fail two of 18 diagnostic checks, and a small rear-deck mark and front-fender sliver remain visible. A prototype improved the rear normal measurements but introduced a visible kink, so it was not applied. The [diagnostic source](evidence/volt-slim-round-2026-10-30/rear-seam-check.gd.txt) is retained. The App run logged several frame hitches.

Reload/reimport and owner/device appearance acceptance remain. No phone test, APK, live account/backend mutation or deployment was performed.
